 {r}←{signal}Process parms;crash;filename;qdmx;TRAP;full;note;⎕IO;⎕ML
⍝ Records the error that is pending (see `⎕DMX`): log entry, Windows event, error WS, component file, custom
⍝ function and HTML page, as far as the parameters ask for them.\\
⍝ After that it signals `signal` if that is not 0; otherwise it `⎕OFF`s if `off` is 1, but only in a runtime or
⍝ with `enforceOff` 1; otherwise it returns. See "Carrying on after an error" in the documentation.\\
⍝ `parms` is a parameter space as created by `CreateParms`: either a reference or its fully qualified name, which
⍝ is what `SetTrap` puts into `⎕TRAP`. An empty vector stands for the defaults, and so does a name that does
⍝ not exist (any more).\\
⍝ `Process` adds variables to the parameter space. Among them are `crashFilename` and `∆ERROR_WS`: both hold the
⍝ name of the crash files without an extension, whether or not the files were written.\\
⍝ Unless `trapInternalErrors` is 0, all actions `Process` will execute are performed under error trapping,
⍝ so it should never fail.\\
⍝ `signal`: if specified this overwrites `parms.signal`, and it stays overwritten; this is for test cases only.\\
⍝ Returns an empty vector as a shy result.
 r←⍬
 TRAP←⎕TRAP                                     ⍝ Before any :Trap of ours: inside one, ⎕TRAP reports that :Trap
 :Hold 'HandleError.Process'
     ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     :Trap 0
         parms←⍎⍣((0≠≢parms)∧(⎕DR parms)∊320 160 80 82)⊣parms ⍝ Convert name into reference
     :Else
         parms←⍬                                ⍝ No such name (any more?): carry on with the defaults
     :EndTrap
     :If 9≠⎕NC'parms'
     :OrIf 0=≢parms
         parms←CreateParms
     :EndIf
     parms←ApplyDefaults parms                  ⍝ A parameter space of an earlier version lacks the newer parameters
     :If 0<⎕NC'signal'
         parms.signal←signal
     :EndIf
     parms.(LastError LastErrorNumber)←qdmx.(DM EN)
     parms.(EN ENX EM Message)←qdmx.(EN ENX EM Message)
     parms.problems←0⍴⊂''                       ⍝ What goes wrong in here; see `AddProblem`
     :Trap parms.trapInternalErrors/0 1000      ⍝ Make sure that it does not crash itself
         parms←CheckErrorFolder parms
         crash←CreateCrashNamespace parms TRAP qdmx
         filename←CreateFilename parms.errorFolder crash
         parms.∆ERROR_WS←filename
         parms.crashFilename←filename
         ⍝ Kill all threads but itself and the main thread - but not in development unless `enforceOff` is 1:
         ⍝ there the session's own threads (Link, Cider, Tatin...) would be killed as well
         {}{0 ⎕TKILL ⍵}⍣(parms.killThreads∧(~APLTreeUtils2.IsDevelopment)∨parms.enforceOff)⊣⎕TNUMS~⎕TID
         (parms full note)←StormGuard parms qdmx       ⍝ `full` is 1 unless the storm guard holds the rest back
         parms←note WriteToLogFile parms
         parms←(note full)WriteToWindowsEvents parms crash ⍝ Both records before ⎕SAVE, the step most likely to fail badly
         :If full
             ⎕DL 0.2
             crash←SaveErrorWorkspace filename parms crash
             crash.Problems←parms.problems
             crash←SaveCrash filename crash parms
             parms←ExecuteCustomFns parms
             WriteHtmlFile parms crash filename
         :EndIf
     :EndTrap
     ⍝ Outside the :Trap: whatever went wrong above, this must still happen
     :If 0≠parms.signal
         ⎕SIGNAL parms.signal
     :ElseIf parms.off
         :If APLTreeUtils2.IsDevelopment∧0=parms.enforceOff
             PrintErrorToSession⊃parms.LastError,⊂'' ⍝ `LastError` is empty when no error was pending
         :Else
             ⎕OFF parms.returnCode
         :EndIf
     :Else
         :If APLTreeUtils2.IsDevelopment∧0=parms.enforceOff
             PrintErrorToSession⊃parms.LastError,⊂'' ⍝ `LastError` is empty when no error was pending
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndHold
⍝Done
